w: 1.~Lord, thee my God, I'll ear- ly seek: my soul doth thirst for thee; My flesh longs in a dry parched land, where- in no wa- ters be:
w: 2.~That I thy po- wer may be- hold, and bright- ness of thy face, As I have seen thee he- re- tofore with- in thy ho- ly place.
w: 3.~Since bet- ter is thy love than life, my lips thee praise shall give. I in thy name will lift my hands, and bless thee while I live.
w: 4.~Ev'n as with mar- row and with fat my soul shall fill- èd be; Then shall my mouth with joy- ful lips sing prais- es un- to thee:
w: 5.~When I do thee up- on my bed re- mem- ber with de- light, And when on thee I me- di- tate in watch- es of the night.
w: 6.~In sha- dow of thy wings I'll joy; for thou mine help hast been. My soul thee fol- lows hard; and me thy right hand doth sus- tain.
w: 7.~Who seek my soul to spill shall sink down to earth's low- est room. They by the sword shall be cut off, and fo- xes' prey be- come.
w: 8.~Yet shall the king in God re- joice, and each one glo- ry shall That swear by him: but stopped shall be the mouth of li- ars all.
